This is a Stage-1 mirror of pygments/pygments (BSD-2-Clause).

Upstream: https://github.com/pygments/pygments
Original author: Georg Brandl and the Pygments team
Upstream license: BSD-2-Clause (see upstream LICENSE, preserved in this tree).

What changed vs upstream (behavior-identical port):
- `pygments/formatters/html.py`: `escape_html` and
  `HtmlFormatter._translate_parts` delegate to the compiled
  `pygments-rust-core` crate (exposed as `pygments._pygments`) when
  present, else the upstream `translate` path. Custom-table calls
  always use the upstream path.
- `pygments/formatters/svg.py`: `escape_html` delegates the same way
  (the replace chain with `&` first is order-equivalent to the
  `translate` mapping); fallback is the upstream chain verbatim.
- `pygments/lexer.py`: `Lexer._preprocess_lexer_input` runs newline
  normalization and tab-expansion/trailing-newline in Rust when
  present; BOM/decoding branches and `strip`/`stripnl`/`stripall`
  stay in Python verbatim. Every other method — `get_tokens`,
  `RegexLexer.get_tokens_unprocessed`, `ExtendedRegexLexer`,
  `DelegatingLexer` — is the upstream source verbatim.
- `pygments/regexopt.py`: `regex_opt` delegates to Rust when present;
  `regex_opt_inner`, `make_charset`, and the fallback path are the
  upstream source verbatim.
- Build backend: hatchling → maturin (PyO3 extension module
  `pygments._pygments`).
